SM(403,{"n":"Deuteronomy 15","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Deuteronomy 15.mp3","d":2301.4,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[23.12,"We're gonna go ahead and get started."],[25.36,"And when we get started in just a moment, uh, we're gonna be picking up at the beginning of chapter 15 of the Book of Deuteronomy."],[34.88,"Once again, we're gonna be able to have a pretty brief catch-up."],[39.12,"This is, as we've now said many times, this is uh Moses' final address uh to the people of Israel on the plains of Moab as they're getting ready to cross the Jordan and go into the land of Canaan under Joshua's leadership."],[54.96,"We are now firmly in the middle of sort of the second section of that address where he's Moses is highlighting and applying and interpreting elements of the commandments that were given in Exodus and Leviticus and Numbers."],[72.44,"So these aren't totally new topics, but Moses is highlighting certain ones that are especially important and talking about ways in which, in some cases, like we saw last time with the tithe and going to the place, the central sanctuary and feasting that."],[94.73,"Some of these are places where things are going to be applied a little differently."],[98.19,"So they've been celebrating the feasts and worshiping and doing all these things in a camp in the desert."],[104.88,"At the tabernacle in the middle of the camp."],[107.04,"Now they're going to be settled across this fair spread of territory."],[112.42,"They don't have ways to travel very quickly."],[115.06,"And so going to the sort of the central, the one central place where the tabernacle and then the temple is going to be, is going to be a more involved process than when it's just in the middle of the camp where you live."],[127.06,"Uh, and certain things are gonna have to work a little differently."],[130.44,"And so some of this is not only being highlighted because it's important, but Moses is sort of reapplying, you know."],[138.2,"We yes, we have a way that was laid out in Leviticus of how we've been doing this."],[143.8,"Here's how we're gonna adapt that."],[146.54,"And then answer.ing related questions"],[148.9,"So, for example, when he said, You don't go and offer sacrifices anywhere except the one place, that raised the question because back in Leviticus, remember it said, if you're gonna kill an animal, you need to sacrifice it."],[165.27,"Uh, you need to offer God, a portion of the meat from the animal."],[170.32,"And so that raised the question well, wait, if we can only do sacrifices at this one place, what if I'm living 120 miles from that place?"],[178.8,"Does that mean I can't eat meat."],[180.98,"Like I can't kill an animal because I'm not gonna be able to sacrifice it."],[185.4,"And so Moses said, No, you can still eat meat."],[188.62,"But you still you don't eat blood."],[190.44,"So he, you know, sort of he's answering those questions."],[194.53,"And giving those those applications."],[198.13,"Um this is an interesting, this theme is interesting to think about it if we pa think about if we pause and think about it for a second, because we've been framing this, and sections of what we've read have very clearly been in this spirit of a farewell address."],[220.23,"Where he talks about how God chose them and loved them and brought them out of Egypt."],[224.39,"They're the kind of things you'd expect, in sort of the final address of a leader."],[229.35,"Who's now preparing for his own death?"],[231.59,"But then there's other things like this. they're sort of very detailed"],[236.03,"How are those two things related?"],[238.59,"Well, in that first case, remember, it wasn't just Moses rehearsing these things for the sake of information."],[249.25,"Then God bringing them out of Egypt, God loving them, and that kind of thing."],[252.37,"There was an application to that."],[254.37,"Remember? It was him exhorting them."],[256.37,"And so you, as God has been faithful to you all these years, you now need to be faithful to God."],[262.3,"So there was an exhortation at the end of that."],[265.1,"A sort of broad, broader exhortation."],[269.02,"In the same way now, when we're talking about these detailed things, this isn't really a different thing."],[276.16,"Because these detailed things are what it means to be faithful to God in return."],[285.08,"Being faithful to God is not just this sort of vague, you know, oh yeah, I love him back."],[294.28,"Yay, God. It's not just this question of feeling or this vague thing."],[300.94,"What Moses is emphasizing is what faithfulness is, is doing all of these quote unquote small things."],[311.08,"Being obedient in all of these day-to-day sort of things."],[316.45,"And that's not really surprising, again, if we think about it a little more, because the most common metaphor that God uses in uh the whole Bible for his relationship with his people is marriage, is a marriage."],[335.65,"And in marriage, being faithful to your spouse, again, is not just a vague thing."],[342.61,"And it's not just like don't commit adultery."],[346.13,"There, I'm I'm faithful."],[347.81,"That's it. That's bare minimum."],[350.01,"Like you don't do that."],[351.37,"But actual faithfulness to your spouse, what is the shape that actually takes every day?"],[357.77,"Shape that takes every day is took out the trash before she had to remind me for the fifth time."],[364.5,"Emptied the dishwasher."],[367.51,"Did this little thing or that little thing to help him or her."],[370.32,"Like that's the shape that that takes every day."],[373.44,"And the same thing is true of our relationship with God."],[376.96,"That's part of what's being communicated here."],[379.3,"That loving God means keeping his commandments."],[382.52,"Loving God means following his ways."],[385.24,"And if these things are little and unimportant."],[387.98,"Then why is it a problem for you to keep them?"],[390.48,"If these are so small and unimportant, it should be easy for you then to just follow them."],[396.04,"Because it's no big deal."],[397.96,"Uh that's sort of the section we're in."],[399.96,"That's the character of the stuff we're currently reading."],[404.08,"So unless there are any leftover comments, uh questions or reminiscences about political corruption of the past, uh, we'll go ahead and pick up in uh Deuteronomy chapter 15, verse one."],[417.04,"At the end of every seven years, you shall grant a remission of debts."],[421.52,"Tip off, this never happened."],[424.56,"Not once. They were supposed to, but it never happened."],[430.32,"Every seven years you shall grant a remission of debts."],[432.72,"So the order of the remission is as follows every debt your neighbor owes you, you shall remit."],[439.44,"You shall not demand it back from your brother, because a remission is proclaimed for the Lord your God."],[445.92,"So let's pause there."],[447.44,"Okay. So notice what the command is."],[449.04,"the The command is not every seven years you get to tell all people you owe money to pound sand."],[457.32,"Uh that'd be nice."],[459.0,"Uh but what it's the opposite of that."],[462.36,"So every seven years, you that's the commandment."],[465.72,"The commandment is to you, you need to forgive every debt that someone owes you."],[475.4,"They never brought the rake back, just let them have the rake, and spend seven years."],[481.1,"So that's that's that's the commandment."],[484.28,"Uh well, so I mean, in this time, uh, because like I mean, I don't have people, I'm not giving people money all the time."],[491.56,"That's yeah, I think's job."],[492.76,"So, like, at this time is it just kind of like you said, like more of a barted situation, or like I mean, and then you talked about before about slavery being used as a system of debt, like right."],[503.68,"Uh so um when he's giving this commandment, is like is the average person like having a loan out?"],[512.16,"I mean, like I guess in the context, indentured servitude was very common."],[516.66,"So think about like Jacob with his uncle Laban, he's I'll work for you for seven years in order to right uh you're not because he didn't have a dowry, to offer."],[526.44,"So what he offered was seven years of his work."],[529.45,"Um, so if you're following this and the seventh year fell three years in, you would say, Okay, I don't you don't need to complete the rest of your contract."],[536.89,"Here's most for most it would be a laboratory"],[543.41,"Those kind of agreements, uh, bartering."],[547.19,"Even so, and you know, just somebody borrowing, and they didn't have currency the way we have it, but they they had precious metals."],[555.41,"And things like that."],[556.71,"Um, that someone might want to borrow or borrow need to borrow food or whatever."],[563.21,"Yeah. Yeah. You may demand it back from a foreigner, but you shall not grant remission of your brother's debt, except when there may be no poor among you."],[579.05,"For the Lord your God will greatly bless you in the land the Lord your God is giving you to possess as an inheritance."],[585.65,"Only if you carefully obey the voice of the Lord your God to observe with care all these commandments, I command you today."],[592.45,"Okay, so he says there's an exception to this."],[598.81,"You can start enforcing debts if there are no poor people in all of Israel."],[606.33,"So as soon as that's taken care of, then you guys can start, you know."],[613.69,"Because now we're just talking about luxury items."],[617.18,"If you guys want to make deals and stuff for luxury items, whatever."],[622.55,"But as long as there is someone in need, you need to be supplying that need without repayment."],[632.67,"Without repayment. And so when, for example, Christ says, to lend without hope of repayment."],[646.45,"This is what he's saying."],[650.35,"He's saying to his disciples, okay, yeah, we all know Israel never did this."],[657.87,"But Christ says, if you're going to be one of his followers, you need to do this."],[663.71,"You do not take someone who is in need and lend them money."],[665.15,"Someone who's starving"],[672.71,"You lend them money to get food expecting to be paid back, especially not with interest."],[678.39,"We're going to see the Old Testament has the death penalty for charging interest."],[690.23,"So did the Israelites at the time, I understand that they did do the debt forgiveness of their own, but did they hold uh foreigners to their debts still?"],[701.43,"Oh, they held everybody to their debts."],[704.15,"They didn't forgive anybody."],[706.79,"But the idea here is you're gonna have the foreigner is a person who's not an Israelite."],[711.49,"So there's someone who's come to work there under some kind of contract."],[716.66,"So a lot of people try to read this as like, oh, it's okay to take advantage of people if they're not Jewish."],[724.51,"That's how a lot of people read this."],[725.95,"But that's not actually, it wouldn't make sense, for someone."],[731.86,"Like, so I'm I'm in a foreign country."],[734.1,"I'm in Moab."],[735.38,"Okay. I'm in Moab."],[737.22,"There's a famine in Moab."],[739.56,"There's not enough food."],[741.2,"There's not work for me to do because the harvests are bad, because there's a famine."],[745.7,"I need to support my family."],[747.38,"So I go and I make a contract in Israel."],[750.9,"I'm gonna come there, I'm gonna work Israeli guys' fields, for X amount of time in return for a room and board for my family and X payment."],[764.33,"So I make that contract."],[766.09,"And then so I move the family, we're all there, and three years later the contract gets voided."],[774.3,"That doesn't make any sense."],[776.84,"Like no one would then do that."],[779.82,"So that would actually be hurting the people, not helping them, by by avoiding all of those contracts."],[787.27,"So that's the idea."],[790.15,"So the idea here is, and this is why God says, after saying, when there's when there are no poor among you, he talks about how he's going to prosper them"],[801.23,"The idea being, God is saying, I'm gonna give you bounty, I'm gonna give you prosperity, you need to share it with each other."],[808.51,"I'm not doing that so that some of you can hoard it away from the others, and that some of you can use it to take advantage of others."],[818.8,"And so, hey, if there's nobody poor, if everybody has the basic necessities of life."],[824.28,"Everybody has what they need for themselves and their families, and you guys want to do all kinds of business deals and stuff, cool."],[832.08,"But first, everybody needs."],[836.1,"Everybody won needs to have their needs met."],[837.46,"This is also important"],[841.34,"Knowing about this passage."],[844.11,"God is saying the goal is that there are no poor among them."],[848.59,"It's important for understanding what Christ says."],[852.51,"Remember what Christ says when the woman has the expensive ointment and oints him with it."],[859.44,"And the disciples and Judas in particular, who of course is stealing from the money box, is super concerned about how much money it was and says, Oh, you could have sold that and given that money to the poor, wink, you know."],[872.81,"And Christ responds sarcastically."],[875.53,"Christ is sarcastic all the time in the New Testament, by the way."],[879.61,"Sarcastically, the poor you will always have with you."],[880.81,"There are weirdos who try to interpret that"],[886.35,"I would say weirdos to be nice."],[888.83,"Who try to interpret that as meaning like, oh, you should try to stop poverty."],[896.35,"Yes, people do."],[898.27,"Yes. Christ said the poor you'll always have with you."],[900.83,"So don't try and eradicate poverty."],[904.13,"Like, yes. It's the opposite."],[909.13,"If you know this, which he explains if you know the Torah, then there should have been no poor in Judea."],[921.27,"If the Jewish people he who Jesus was talking to, like Judas and his disciples, if they had been keeping the Torah, there would not be any poor people needing that money."],[935.01,"And so he's being ironic about, oh yeah, now you're really worried about the poor, huh?"],[942.05,"What what have you been doing about that like previously?"],[949.27,"And so saying the poor you always have with you means essentially, you've never obeyed this, and I know you guys, you never will."],[958.39,"That's a pretty harsh indictment."],[960.99,"What Christ is saying there."],[962.76,"You're never gonna do what you're supposed to be doing."],[965.88,"And so, yes, as we know, this didn't forgive their debts"],[969.76,"Um, but this is also so a lot of the language, the reason why uh in Christ's teaching, you get a lot of the language of debt being used to talk about the forgiveness of sins is also connected to this."],[985.36,"It's a way of interpreting these parts of the Torah."],[988.65,"That yes, it meant literally you were supposed to forgive monetary debts, but that's also an image that was supposed to give you this deeper spiritual understanding of forgiving others in general."],[1004.59,"In general. And so if we understand this in Deuteronomy that way, that is the larger meaning"],[1014.16,"You don't have to wait every seven years to forgive people."],[1018.37,"But that would probably better that be better than a lot of our average records."],[1025.49,"I've been ticked off about something for more than seven years."],[1031.73,"In the past."],[1033.23,"Like, there's a moratorium."],[1035.79,"There's a point where you have to let it go."],[1039.64,"There's a point where you have to forgive and move on."],[1045.16,"And that's really what it's saying."],[1046.48,"Because it says, remember, you have to forgive your brother his debt."],[1050.6,"Doesn't say you have to talk to him."],[1051.88,"Just says you have to scratch it off the books"],[1052.24,"Does it say you have to."],[1057.25,"And just not worry about it."],[1059.49,"And so that idea of forgiveness of letting go, not holding on to everything forever."],[1072.77,"You shall lend to many nations, but you shall not borrow."],[1077.01,"You shall rule over many nations, but they shall not rule over you."],[1087.81,"God is saying to them that he set them free from Egypt."],[1093.97,"Egypt ruled over them."],[1095.41,"them. God set free from that"],[1096.57,"Egypt held them in slavery."],[1098.83,"In debt. They're not going to do that."],[1103.95,"They're not to do that again."],[1105.31,"They're not to enter back into that kind of subjugation and that kind of slavery."],[1112.45,"Now that makes sense, but how does that relate to what we were just talking about?"],[1117.09,"That seems like the opposite of what we were just talking about."],[1124.05,"And that's because the idea here, what connects those two is that the failure to forgive, the failure to let go of things actually enslaves you."],[1142.73,"You think because I'm holding on to this."],[1146.83,"Because I won't let go of it, I am still above this other person who I won't forgive, who I won't let off the hook, who I won't."],[1154.88,"But the exact opposite is what becomes the case."],[1160.45,"This is in Deuteronomy."],[1161.65,"Fuerbach only figured it out in the 19th century."],[1164.74,"But that's like one percent of the eventual audience of this will get that reference."],[1170.26,"But right, so that's the idea here."],[1173.56,"Is that there's actually an inversion."],[1176.7,"When you won't forgive, you end up getting held hostage by who and what you won't forgive."],[1182.38,"Yeah Not the other way around."],[1187.3,"You can't move on."],[1189.78,"You're the one who's actually trapped."],[1193.14,"If there is among you a poor man of your brethren, if."],[1199.39,"Because there's not supposed to be."],[1201.36,"If there is among you a poor man of your brethren within any of the cities in your land, the Lord your God is giving you, you shall not harden your heart, nor shut your hand from your poor brother, but you shall surely open your hands to him and willingly lend him sufficient for his need, whatever he needs."],[1220.08,"Beware lest there be a hidden thought in your heart, a transgression of the law, saying the seventh year, the year of remission is at hand, and your eye be evil against your poor brother, and you give him nothing."],[1235.08,"We'll pause there a second."],[1236.68,"Okay. God knows how we are."],[1239.9,"Oh, wait, next year's the year where I have to I'm not I can't give it to him now."],[1245.34,"I won't get it back."],[1248.38,"When the new side, yeah, when the new cycle starts, then, you know, because I can try and get it back before I have to forget."],[1254.2,"He he knows."],[1255.16,"And and but notice what it says."],[1256.84,"It says it's a that's a transgression of the law."],[1261.0,"Doesn't sound like it."],[1262.06,"It sounds like technically you're following it."],[1266.47,"Like, technically. You're speaking shrewd about it."],[1269.83,"This is what St"],[1270.64,"Uh, because again, God knows how we are."],[1275.33,"Paul is talking about with the letter of the law and the spirit of the law."],[1279.73,"This is what Christ is talking about to the Pharisees when he says, you tithe of min to dill and cub, like they're their herb garden, cutting out like 10%, like little scissors."],[1288.79,"He says, but you neglect things like mercy, righteousness."],[1294.65,"You ignore those things."],[1295.94,"Because you're just concerned about following the rule, and you have to do both."],[1301.0,"This isn't a new thing."],[1302.92,"And so, this isn't this new thing that Christ brings or that Christianity brings that, like, oh no, now you have to also."],[1311.48,"Okay That's right here from the beginning."],[1315.12,"If you're trying to think of a way to get around God's commandment, you've already broken it."],[1321.12,"Like, that's it."],[1323.62,"That's it. It is already broken."],[1326.66,"And so there is no, you know, you don't you don't get a lawyer or even to be one when you stand before the judgment seat of Christ."],[1335.32,"You don't get representation like that."],[1337.64,"Um, where they're gonna be like, well, technically the statute says that's not how it works."],[1343.82,"That's not how it works."],[1345.5,"Idea is you need to help this poor person."],[1349.42,"Period. With everything, with everything he needs."],[1355.55,"You think to yourself, the seventh year, the year of remission is at hand, and your eye be evil against your brother, and you give him nothing, and he cry out to the Lord against you, and it be a great sin among you."],[1370.03,"You shall surely give him and loan him as much as he needs, and your heart should not be grieved when you give to him."],[1377.63,"Because for this thing, the Lord your God will bless you in all your works, and in everything to which you put your hand."],[1385.39,"For the poor will never cease from the land."],[1388.51,"Wait, he just said there weren't supposed to be any."],[1391.47,"Yeah. But he also knew."],[1396.91,"Therefore, I command you to do this word, which says. you shall surely open your hands to your brother, to your poor and needy in your land"],[1407.27,"So whenever I've seen this in the past, the way I made sense of it before was that um there are people who like don't there are people who want to be like homeless and stuff like that."],[1419.75,"Like you can't, like that's their their choice in life, and there's no way away that at least I've seen that you can resolve that issue."],[1428.79,"If somebody wants to, you know, live in those ways, then it's like what it what is the I mean, because I mean that's a real situation that we have when like they're different states are dealing with different ways, and there's all this we've got a lot of political network around how to handle all that."],[1443.83,"And so I mean well nob hereody's a government official so we don't need to worry about that part right I well I don't know but I mean I mean you can see that there is like a a genuine like people trying to figure out how to resolve these situations and I mean uh I I mean they're other than giving alms like well I mean that's ultimately it you have what is within your power to do and that's what you're responsible for and I mean we know we know the difference right this isn't saying like oh I need to move out of my house and keep paying the rent and let some homeless person live there instead while I'm homeless."],[1478.83,"Like this isn't this isn't even sell everything you have and give it to the poor."],[1483.49,"This isn't even that."],[1485.09,"This is just right, don't harden your heart and don't close your hand."],[1490.55,"And and we know the difference and we've all done both."],[1493.91,"We've seen people and hardened our hearts and gone past them and not helped them."],[1497.51,"And I'm pretty confident that everybody here at one point or another has helped someone."],[1501.6,"When they could."],[1502.72,"And so God is saying to do one and not the other."],[1506.64,"But you can't do like it's not within my power to like give somebody a job."],[1514.82,"Like I don't have jobs to give."],[1517.64,"Um, it's not within my power."],[1519.64,"If it was, then it would behoove me to try to help people who are in need."],[1524.48,"Like if I ran a construction company."],[1527.49,"And I needed I needed labor."],[1529.57,"or. Like it would behoove me to find po out of work people and offer them jobs"],[1534.75,"Because that would be within my power."],[1536.43,"But I don't."],[1538.0,"But I mean, I can you don't have to do it in stupid ways either."],[1543.52,"It doesn't always mean handing somebody money."],[1546.16,"Not that that even is always wrong, but right, just it does all uh, you know, the the time I most get approached by people, frankly, is when I'm walking into a store."],[1558.53,"And it's very easy as I walk into a store to say, like, hey, do you need something from the store?"],[1566.53,"Buy him a bottle of water, buy him a sandwich, buy, you know, hand it to him on my way out."],[1571.19,"Like, that that's not hard to do."],[1571.59,"'s not that hard to do. And so God is just saying, it"],[1574.27,"And most of the time I'm able to do it."],[1579.63,"You're able to do it."],[1581.31,"So do it."],[1583.51,"But the key part here, and I think even the way it's translated here, people aren't going to read it correctly."],[1591.29,"So where it says, Because for this thing the Lord your God will bless you at all your works and in everything to which you put your hand."],[1600.73,"I think people read that in this weird quasi-prosperity gospel way."],[1604.89,"That, like, oh, if you help the poor person, then God will bless you and give you money in return."],[1609.77,"It's the exact opposite in the original, both of the Hebrew and the Greek."],[1614.57,"The reason you're supposed to help is because God blessed you so that you would be able to help him."],[1627.41,"So if God has given you wealth or influence, whatever God has given you, he hasn't given that to you just because he loves you better than everybody else and wants you to have this great wealthy lifestyle."],[1639.01,"He's done that for you so that you can help those in need."],[1643.25,"Basically, like talents."],[1645.01,"Yeah. That's why he gave it to you."],[1647.99,"That's what it's saying."],[1649.67,"That's why God gave you that money so that you could give it to this person in need."],[1654.81,"And so if you keep it, what does that mean?"],[1659.97,"That's the idea right behind the commandment."],[1664.37,"God gave it to you so that you could help this person, and instead you decided to keep it for yourself for your own enjoyment and let that person suffer."],[1689.71,"God is saying, it's still mine."],[1692.43,"But I'm entrusting it to you."],[1693.87,"And if you do the things here that the people you're displacing did, you're gonna be out of here too."],[1700.11,"And someone else will come in and take it."],[1703.07,"The same thing is true with the bounty of the land, the wealth of the land that it's gonna produce."],[1708.63,"That's God's too."],[1712.79,"And so he's saying in this chapter, I'm in I'm giving that to all of you."],[1720.95,"And on any given harvest season, it's not gonna be perfectly evenly distributed."],[1727.21,"And that means you guys are gonna have to do that."],[1733.05,"Those of you who do really well are gonna have to help the ones who don't do as well."],[1739.61,"And the ones who don't do as well are gonna have to humble yourselves and receive help from those who did who did better."],[1747.71,"On both sides."],[1752.35,"But the ones who did well are the ones who are in control of the situation."],[1757.95,"They're the ones who face the temptation, the biggest temptation."],[1762.13,"They have the power to share or the power not to."],[1767.65,"And that's why they're the ones who who are being primarily addressed here."],[1772.45,"But notice also, this is something we've already seen a bit in the Torah."],[1776.93,"We're gonna see more in Deuteronomy."],[1778.93,"This idea of if you're hardened your heart, he's gonna cry out to God against you."],[1784.05,"And God's saying he's God's gonna listen to that."],[1788.13,"And that's calling us back to think about Abel's blood, calling out to God from the ground."],[1793.95,"Think about that, you know, you may think, oh, nobody cares about that person."],[1802.27,"I don't have to worry about that."],[1803.55,"I don't have to."],[1804.87,"Lazarus out there at my gates, who cares about him?"],[1808.41,"Well, God is saying God cares about him."],[1813.37,"God cares about him."],[1815.13,"And so the idea here, the idea of calling out."],[1818.15,"If you knew some kid was an incredibly rich person's son, you would not walk up and smack that kid, saying."],[1830.6,"And that kid asked you for help, and you knew this was. a uh wealthy and influential, powerful person's son, you would help them"],[1840.54,"You would not take advantage of that kid, you would not abuse that kid."],[1845.78,"Well, that person who you think is a nobody, God is saying is God's son."],[1854.02,"And so the way you treat them reflects on what you think of and how you feel about God."],[1866.38,"It's almost like that whole sheep and goats thing we read about last week."],[1871.06,"was It already here in Deuteronomy, basically."],[1874.02,"If your brother, a Hebrew man or a Hebrew woman, is sold to you and serves you six years, then in the seventh year you shall let him go free from you."],[1885.5,"But when you send him away free from you, you shall not let him go away empty handed."],[1890.62,"You shall supply him liberally from your sheep, wheat, and wine press."],[1895.9,"From what the Lord has blessed you with, you shall give to him."],[1899.66,"So this is talking about contract ends, or we get to the seven years and it ends."],[1907.82,"It's not just like, well, okay, nice having you work for me."],[1911.26,"Good luck in your future endeavors."],[1912.94,"See ya. Because what's gonna happen now?"],[1920.51,"He's got a year before he can go get another work contract."],[1928.6,"So no, you don't just toss him out the front door."],[1934.33,"You give him"],[1936.15,"Uh you give him severance pay."],[1937.84,"You give him things to Titan until he can."],[1941.28,"I get a job to provide for himself and his family."],[1943.92,"Why? Because he's your brother or sister."],[1954.8,"Which implies here already, even though we're literally talking about slaves, not really your property."],[1962.64,"No, it doesn't"],[1963.56,"You remember that when people say, Oh, the Bible says his slavery is good."],[1968.28,"Not once. Not once."],[1972.78,"This person is your brother."],[1974.46,"This is not really that different than what St."],[1976.38,"Paul says in Philemon."],[1979.26,"When he says to Philemon, this person is your brother in Christ."],[1983.74,"How can you claim to own him?"],[1989.2,"This is the same thing."],[1990.4,"He's your brother."],[1993.6,"Okay, so you're not just cutting him loose."],[1996.16,"You need to help him for that year."],[1997.92,"He now needs help."],[1998.88,"So you you help him."],[2000.64,"Because God's given you."],[2002.0,"Clearly, if you've got servants, you're doing pretty well."],[2005.66,"So you can help provide for him."],[2009.86,"You shall remember you were a servant in the land of Egypt, and the Lord your God redeemed you from that place."],[2017.06,"Therefore, I command you this thing."],[2020.18,"But if he says to you, I will not go away from you, because he loves you in your house, because he is well off with you, then you shall take a small awl and pierce his ear at the door, and he shall be your servant forever."],[2034.66,"Also to your female servant, you shall do likewise."],[2039.38,"So what is this saying?"],[2040.42,"So this is saying, remember, the onus is this person had to make this contract, had to sell themselves to me, essentially."],[2048.82,"This person incurred a debt to me"],[2051.78,"I have to forgive that debt."],[2052.82,"This isn't an onus put on them"],[2054.22,"I have to let them free from slavery."],[2059.0,"So that seventh year comes that I say, okay, well, you're free to go."],[2063.64,"And they say, No, I like living here."],[2067.08,"I like working here."],[2068.2,"I like being part of this family."],[2069.89,"I want to stay here."],[2070.69,"This is where I want to."],[2071.81,"You and my family want to be here for the rest of our lives."],[2075.55,"You don't throw them out."],[2078.65,"No, be gone, peasant."],[2080.03,"No. They can become part of the family."],[2081.97,"And so there is a then a ritual here, which is a shortened version."],[2086.69,"We talked about this more in Exodus."],[2088.21,"So you can roll back there to get the more detailed discussion."],[2090.93,"But this is referring back to that, this piercing of the ear."],[2094.37,"this They are now part of family."],[2101.05,"Which means they still have a different relationship."],[2106.97,"It isn't, well, then their debt remains forever."],[2110.25,"They're not there as an indentured servant anymore."],[2114.25,"They're there willingly."],[2116.01,"And they're part of the family."],[2118.42,"So that relationship has still shifted in this situation."],[2127.86,"It shall not seem hard to you when you send him away free from you."],[2131.86,"For he has worked the yearly wage of a hired servant in serving you six years."],[2136.9,"Then the Lord your God will bless you in all you do."],[2140.78,"So that's this last bit is a little shifted topic."],[2145.28,"But that's all about the Sabbath year and debt forgiveness."],[2151.04,"Now we're moving topics."],[2152.48,"All the firstborn males that come from your oxen and sheep, you shall sanctify to the Lord your God."],[2158.32,"You shall do no work with the firstborn young bull, nor shear the firstborn of your sheep."],[2170.32,"Well, that is, uh, you give them to God right away as a sacrifice."],[2176.64,"Again, God knows us."],[2179.84,"Well, oh, hey, look, this is the firstborn male."],[2182.8,"This is a very bull."],[2183.84,"Okay, well, we'll get some work out of him, and then when he's old and feeble, we'll go ahead and haul him down to the down to the temple and then we'll give him to God."],[2195.34,"Or, well, we'll just we'll just keep the sheep for a few seasons and shear them and keep the wool, and then we'll, you know, once we've done that, then we'll go and we'll give them God."],[2205.02,"And you hear, no."],[2207.58,"Immediately when they're born, you take them and and you give them to God."],[2213.74,"You and your household shall eat it before the Lord year by year in the place the Lord your God chooses."],[2220.46,"But if there is a defect in it, if it is lame or blind or has any serious defect, you shall not sacrifice it to the Lord your God."],[2228.74,"You may eat it within your cities, the unclean and the clean person alike may eat it, as if it were a gazelle or a deer."],[2235.38,"Well, you shall not eat its blood, you shall pour it on the ground like water."],[2239.14,"Okay, so this is again a very specific ruling."],[2242.34,"Well, what if the firstborn one comes out and you know uh there's a defect where it hasn't died yet, but probably will, or just in general."],[2254.07,"And so that is you don't offer that one to God."],[2256.63,"You wait for the next one that's born, the firstborn that's healthy."],[2261.97,"And well, that's the animal that you sacrifice."],[2264.93,"And it says, but that other one that was defective in some way, you can still eat it, you just don't sacrifice it."],[2272.7,"As with all of these, when you eat it, you have to drain the blood."],[2278.86,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2286.3,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2291.58,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":23.12,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: Moses' second address","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at <b>Deuteronomy 15:1</b>; brief catch-up</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Moses' final address</b> on the plains of Moab, about to cross Jordan under <b>Joshua</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Now in the <b>second section</b>: highlighting, applying, interpreting commandments from <b>Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not totally new topics - ones that are <b>especially important</b></li><li class=\"d1\">some will be <b>applied differently</b> (last time: tithe, central sanctuary, feasting)</li><li class=\"d0\">Before: feasts and worship in a <b>camp in the desert</b>, tabernacle in the middle</li><li class=\"d1\">now settled over a spread of territory, <b>no fast travel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">going to the one central place = a more <b>involved process</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So Moses <b>re-applies</b>: \"here's how we're gonna adapt that\" and answers related questions</li></ul>"},{"t":148.9,"lv":3,"h":"Example: eating meat away from the sanctuary","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Leviticus: kill an animal → <b>sacrifice it</b>, offer God a portion</li><li class=\"d0\">Only one place for sacrifice → \"what if I'm living <b>120 miles</b> from that place?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"does that mean I can't eat meat?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: <b>you can still eat meat</b> - but <b>don't eat blood</b></li></ul>"},{"t":198.13,"lv":2,"h":"Why detail follows farewell","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Sections so far = <b>farewell address</b>: God <b>chose, loved, brought them out of Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d1\">what you'd expect from a leader preparing for his death</li><li class=\"d0\">Then very <b>detailed</b> stuff - how are they related?</li><li class=\"d0\">First part was <b>exhortation</b>, not just information</li><li class=\"d1\">God was faithful to you → <b>you now be faithful to God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Detailed things = <b>what faithfulness means</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a vague feeling - \"oh yeah, I love him back. Yay, God.\"</li><li class=\"d1\">faithfulness = doing all these \"<b>small things</b>\", day-to-day obedience</li></ul>"},{"t":316.45,"lv":3,"h":"Marriage and the small things","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Most common <b>biblical metaphor</b> for God and his people = <b>marriage</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Faithfulness to a spouse is not just \"don't commit <b>adultery</b>\" - bare minimum</li><li class=\"d1\">real shape each day: <b>took out the trash</b> before she reminded me the fifth time; emptied the dishwasher</li><li class=\"d0\">Same with God: <b>loving God = keeping his commandments</b>, following his ways</li><li class=\"d0\">If they're <b>small and unimportant</b> → why a problem to keep them? Should be easy</li></ul>"},{"t":404.08,"lv":2,"h":"Deuteronomy 15:1-3 - Remission of debts","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reads 15:1-3</b>: every <b>seven years</b> a remission of debts</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Tip off: <b>this never happened</b>. Not once.\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Order: every debt your neighbor owes you, <b>remit</b>; don't demand it back from your brother</li><li class=\"d0\">Notice the command: not \"tell everyone you owe to <b>pound sand</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the opposite: <b>you forgive</b> what others owe you</li><li class=\"d1\">\"they never brought the rake back, just let them have the rake\"</li></ul>"},{"t":484.28,"lv":3,"h":"Q: Who was lending in those days?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: average person having a loan out? <b>slavery as a system of debt</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Indentured servitude</b> very common</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jacob and Laban</b>: no dowry, so offered <b>seven years of work</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if the seventh year fell three years in, \"you don't need to complete the rest of your contract\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Most agreements = <b>labor, bartering</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Also borrowing: <b>precious metals</b>, food - no currency like ours</li></ul>"},{"t":563.21,"lv":2,"h":"Deuteronomy 15:3-6 - No poor among you","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reads 15:3-6</b>: may demand from a <b>foreigner</b>, not from your brother, \"except when there may be <b>no poor among you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God will <b>greatly bless</b> you in the land - <b>only if</b> you obey</li><li class=\"d0\">Exception: enforce debts if <b>no poor in all Israel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">then only <b>luxury items</b> - make deals if you like</li><li class=\"d1\">while someone is in need, supply the need <b>without repayment</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ: \"<b>lend without hope of repayment</b>\" - this is what he means</li><li class=\"d1\">everyone knew Israel never did this; <b>his followers must</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't lend to someone <b>starving</b> expecting payback, \"especially not with interest\"</li><li class=\"d1\">OT has the <b>death penalty for charging interest</b> (more later)</li></ul>"},{"t":690.23,"lv":3,"h":"Q: Were foreigners held to their debts?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: did Israelites hold foreigners to debts?</li><li class=\"d0\">\"They held <b>everybody</b> to their debts. They didn't forgive anybody.\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Foreigner</b> = non-Israelite, here under some <b>contract</b></li><li class=\"d1\">many read it as \"ok to take advantage of non-Jews\" - <b>doesn't make sense</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Scenario: <b>famine in Moab</b>, no work → I contract to work Israeli fields for room, board, payment</li><li class=\"d1\">three years later contract <b>voided</b>? Hurts the foreigner, not helps</li></ul>"},{"t":790.15,"lv":3,"h":"God's purpose: bounty shared","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">After \"no poor among you\" he talks of <b>prospering them</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God: \"I'm gonna give you <b>bounty</b> - <b>share it</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not so some can <b>hoard</b> it or <b>take advantage</b> of others</li><li class=\"d0\">If everybody has <b>basic necessities</b> → do all the business deals you want</li><li class=\"d1\">\"first, <b>everybody's needs met</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":837.46,"lv":3,"h":"\"The poor you will always have\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Goal: <b>no poor among them</b> - key to understanding Christ</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Woman with expensive ointment</b>; disciples and <b>Judas</b> (stealing from the money box): \"sell it, give to the poor\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ responds <b>sarcastically</b> (\"sarcastic all the time in the NT\") - the poor you will always have</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Weirdos\" read it as <b>don't try to stop poverty</b> - \"it's the opposite\"</li><li class=\"d1\">if you knew the Torah, there <b>should have been no poor in Judea</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ironic</b>: \"now you're worried about the poor? What have you been doing?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">= \"you've <b>never obeyed this</b>, and you never will\" - a <b>harsh indictment</b></li></ul>"},{"t":969.76,"lv":2,"h":"Debt as the language of forgiveness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Christ's <b>debt language</b> for forgiveness of sins connects here</li><li class=\"d0\">Way of interpreting the Torah: literally forgive <b>monetary debts</b>, also an image of <b>forgiving others generally</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Don't wait every seven years - \"I've been ticked off for <b>more than seven years</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"a <b>moratorium</b>... a point where you have to let it go\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Says forgive his debt - doesn't say you have to <b>talk to him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"just <b>scratch it off the books</b>\" and not worry about it</li><li class=\"d1\">idea of <b>letting go</b>, not holding on forever</li></ul>"},{"t":1072.77,"lv":2,"h":"Deuteronomy 15:6 - Lend, don't borrow","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reads 15:6</b>: <b>lend to many nations, not borrow</b>; rule over many, not ruled over</li><li class=\"d0\">God freed them from Egypt - <b>slavery, in debt</b>; not to return to <b>subjugation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Seems the opposite of forgiveness - how connected?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>failure to forgive enslaves you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'm still <b>above</b> him, won't let him off the hook\" - the opposite happens</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Feuerbach only figured it out in the 19th century\" - in Deuteronomy already</li><li class=\"d0\">Inversion: won't forgive → <b>held hostage</b> by who and what you won't forgive</li><li class=\"d1\">you can't move on; you're the one <b>trapped</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1193.14,"lv":2,"h":"Deuteronomy 15:7-11 - Open your hand","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reads 15:7-9</b>: \"<b>if</b> there is a poor man\" - there's not supposed to be</li><li class=\"d1\">don't <b>harden your heart</b> or shut your hand; lend sufficient for his need</li><li class=\"d1\">beware the <b>hidden thought</b>: \"the seventh year is at hand\" → eye evil, give nothing</li><li class=\"d0\">God knows how we are: \"next year I can't give it - <b>won't get it back</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">he calls it a <b>transgression of the law</b>; technically you're following it, shrewdly</li><li class=\"d0\">= <b>letter vs spirit</b> (St Paul)</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ to Pharisees: tithe <b>mint, dill, cumin</b> - \"little scissors\" - neglect <b>mercy, righteousness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">do <b>both</b> - \"not a new thing Christianity brings\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1315.12,"lv":3,"h":"No lawyers at the judgment seat","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">If you're finding a way around the commandment, \"you've <b>already broken it</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">At Christ's judgment seat: \"you don't get a <b>lawyer</b>\" - \"technically the statute says...\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Idea: <b>help this poor person. Period.</b> With everything he needs</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reads 15:9-11</b>: he cries to the Lord → <b>great sin</b></li><li class=\"d1\">give as much as he needs; heart <b>not grieved</b>; the Lord will bless</li><li class=\"d1\">\"the poor will <b>never cease</b> from the land\" - he just said none; \"<b>he also knew</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1407.27,"lv":3,"h":"Q: What about the homeless by choice?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: some people <b>choose to be homeless</b>; states, politics, no way to resolve it; only almsgiving?</li><li class=\"d0\">A: \"you have what is <b>within your power</b>, and that's what you're responsible for\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"move out of my house and let a homeless person live there\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not even <b>sell everything and give to the poor</b></li><li class=\"d1\">just: <b>don't harden your heart, don't close your hand</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"We've all done both\" - passed by, and helped</li><li class=\"d0\">Not within his power to give jobs - if he ran a <b>construction company</b>, it would be</li><li class=\"d0\">Don't do it in <b>stupid ways</b>: not always handing money</li><li class=\"d1\">walking into a store: \"do you need something?\" → <b>bottle of water, a sandwich</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"You're able to do it. So do it.\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1583.51,"lv":2,"h":"Blessed in order to help","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Read wrongly as <b>prosperity gospel</b>: help the poor, God gives you money back</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Opposite</b> in Hebrew and Greek: <b>God blessed you so that you'd be able to help</b></li><li class=\"d1\">wealth or influence not because he loves you better, for a <b>great lifestyle</b></li><li class=\"d1\">given \"so you can help those in need\" - <b>like talents</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Keep it? → used for your own enjoyment while the person suffers</li><li class=\"d0\">\"It's still <b>mine</b>, entrusted to you\"</li><li class=\"d1\">do what the <b>displaced nations</b> did → you're out too, someone else takes it</li><li class=\"d0\">Same with the <b>bounty of the land</b> - God's too</li><li class=\"d1\">harvest <b>not evenly distributed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doing well → <b>help</b> the ones who don't; those who don't → <b>humble themselves</b> and receive</li><li class=\"d1\">those who did well face the <b>biggest temptation</b> - power to share or not - so primarily addressed</li></ul>"},{"t":1772.45,"lv":3,"h":"He cries out against you","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Hardened heart → <b>he'll cry out to God against you</b>; God listens</li><li class=\"d1\">recalls <b>Abel's blood</b> crying from the ground</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Nobody cares about <b>Lazarus at my gate</b>\" - God cares</li><li class=\"d0\">Illustration: an <b>incredibly rich person's son</b> asks for help - you'd never abuse him</li><li class=\"d1\">the \"nobody\" is <b>God's son</b> → how you treat him reflects how you feel about God</li><li class=\"d0\">\"That whole <b>sheep and goats</b> thing we read last week - already here in Deuteronomy\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1866.38,"lv":2,"h":"Deuteronomy 15:12-15 - Releasing servants","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reads 15:12-14</b>: Hebrew man or woman sold to you, serves <b>six years</b>, free in the <b>seventh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't send him <b>empty-handed</b>: supply liberally from <b>sheep, wheat, winepress</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"good luck in your future endeavors. See ya.\"</li><li class=\"d1\">he has <b>a year</b> before another work contract</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>severance pay</b> until he can provide for himself and family</li><li class=\"d1\">why: <b>he's your brother or sister</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Though \"literally slaves\" - not really <b>property</b></li><li class=\"d1\">when people say \"the Bible says slavery is good\" - <b>not once</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>Philemon</b>: \"your brother in Christ - how can you claim to own him?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">If you have servants you're doing well → <b>you can help</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>15:15</b>: remember you were a <b>servant in Egypt</b>, the Lord redeemed you</li></ul>"},{"t":2020.18,"lv":3,"h":"Deuteronomy 15:16-18 - The pierced ear","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reads 15:16-17</b>: if he says \"I won't go away\" → <b>awl through the ear</b> at the door; servant forever; same for female servant</li><li class=\"d0\">Onus: he sold himself to me, incurred a <b>debt</b>; I must forgive it and <b>free him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if he says \"I like it here, part of this family\" → don't throw him out</li><li class=\"d1\">becomes <b>part of the family</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ritual</b> = shortened version; fuller in <b>Exodus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">relationship still <b>shifted</b>: not indentured anymore, there <b>willingly</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>15:18</b>: shouldn't seem hard - he worked <b>six years at a hired servant's wage</b>; God will bless you</li><li class=\"d0\">Last bit a shifted topic: all about the <b>Sabbath year</b> and debt forgiveness</li></ul>"},{"t":2151.04,"lv":2,"h":"Deuteronomy 15:19-23 - Firstborn animals","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Moving topics\": <b>reads 15:19</b>: all firstborn males of oxen and sheep → <b>sanctify to the Lord</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no work with the firstborn bull, no shearing the firstborn sheep</li><li class=\"d0\">Means: give them to God <b>right away</b> as a sacrifice</li><li class=\"d0\">God knows us: \"we'll get some work out of him, then haul him to the temple when <b>old and feeble</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">or \"keep the sheep a few seasons for the <b>wool</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"no\" - <b>immediately when they're born</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>15:20</b>: eat it before the Lord <b>year by year</b> in the place he chooses</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>15:21-23</b>: defect - lame, blind, serious → <b>don't sacrifice</b></li><li class=\"d1\">eat it within your cities, <b>clean and unclean alike</b>, \"as a gazelle or a deer\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>don't eat the blood</b> - pour it on the ground like water</li><li class=\"d0\">Specific ruling: firstborn with a defect → <b>wait for the next healthy firstborn</b> to sacrifice</li><li class=\"d1\">always <b>drain the blood</b></li></ul>"}]});
